From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: sun60i-a733: remove the root port's VPD capability

Every lspci -vvv on the board logs

  pcieport 0000:00:00.0: VPD access failed.  This is likely a firmware bug
  on this device.  Contact the card vendor for a firmware update

(6 GB board, 2026-09-21). The
root port, 1f6d:abcd, lists a VPD capability, and the PCI core then polls its
flag until pci_vpd_wait() gives up after 125 ms.

WHY IT FAILS

In the DesignWare core VPD is not implemented, it is delegated. UM V1.00
18.3.8.62 (SII_INT_0, bit 0 PF0_CFG_VPD_INT, p. 1236): the controller only
pulses cfg_vpd_int; the integrating application must then read the VPD
Control/Capabilities register, move the four bytes, and set or clear the
VPD flag to complete the request. The feature list (18.3.1, p. 1178)
names VPD as a capability of the core, not as a store.

Nothing on the A733 is that application. The User Defined Space has no VPD
register, the UM describes no VPD store, and `pci-sun60i-a733-root-port-event-irq-on-sii`'s SII handler serves the
root-port event bits, not bit 0. So the flag never flips and every access
times out.

THE FIX

One call in `pci-sun60i-a733-root-port-event-irq-on-sii`'s sun60i_a733_pcie_host_init(), beside its MSI and MSI-X
removals: dw_pcie_remove_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_VPD). host_init runs
before dw_pcie_setup_rc() and before enumeration, and the helper opens DBI
read-only writes itself. pci_vpd_init() then finds no capability, the vpd
attribute in sysfs is not created (vpd_attr_is_visible()), and lspci has
nothing to read.

Scoped to this compatible on purpose. A PCI quirk would have to key on the
port's ID, 1f6d:abcd, which is a placeholder, not an allocation.

DEPENDS ON `pci-sun60i-a733-root-port-event-irq-on-sii`

This edits the host_init that `pci-sun60i-a733-root-port-event-irq-on-sii` creates and does not apply without it.
Apply order: the event-IRQ patch first, then this one.

VERIFIED

Applies at fuzz 0 on main + `pci-sun60i-a733-root-port-event-irq-on-sii`; compile-check passes, and the built
object calls dw_pcie_remove_capability with 3 = PCI_CAP_ID_VPD from
sun60i_a733_pcie_host_init. NOT hardware-proven. The observable: lspci -vvv
-s 00:00.0 lists no "Vital Product Data" capability and the kernel logs no
"VPD access failed"; /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:00:00.0/vpd does not exist.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -375,6 +375,15 @@
 	dw_pcie_remove_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_MSI);
 	dw_pcie_remove_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_MSIX);
 
+	/*
+	 * VPD is advertised and nothing serves it. The DesignWare core only
+	 * pulses cfg_vpd_int (SII_INT_0 bit 0, UM V1.00 18.3.8.62) and leaves
+	 * the transfer and the VPD flag to an application the A733 does not
+	 * have, so every access times out in pci_vpd_wait() with "VPD access
+	 * failed". Unlinked, the port says what is true: it has no VPD.
+	 */
+	dw_pcie_remove_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_VPD);
+
 	pcie->exp_cap = dw_pcie_find_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP);
 	pcie->aer_cap = dw_pcie_find_ext_capability(pci, PCI_EXT_CAP_ID_ERR);
 
